    "lawCode": "Add §817, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5650A\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to expanding access to\nadvanced courses to improve educational equity\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill seeks to expand access to advanced courses to improve educa-\ntional equity.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds a new section 817 to education law that provides for\nnotice to parents on the availability of and information on advanced\ncourses. Such notice shall include the benefits of participating of AP\ncourses, a description of the courses offered in the current and follow-\ning school years by a district or charter school and how to prepare and\nenroll in them, and a description of the academic and non-academic\nsupport the district or charter school provides including financial\nassistance relating to the cost of participating in AP courses. Such\nnotice will be provided electronically or by mail and be posted on the\nwebsite of the district or charter school.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nStudies have revealed a lack of equity in enrollment of students in\nadvanced courses. A recent study found that even when they scored profi-\ncient on the state math assessment in grade 7, students who are low-in-\ncome or students of color were less likely than their peers to be\nenrolled in an advanced math class in grade 9. Furthermore, in 2018-19,\nhigh school students in New York State who were low-income or students\nof color were approximately half as likely to be enrolled in advanced\ncourses including Physics, Calculus, Computer Science, Advanced Place-\nment (AP) and International Baccalaureate (IS).\n\nThis bill seeks to address this inequity by ensuring that families and\nstudents are aware of the advanced course offerings at their school.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS1111A of 2021-22: REFERRED TO EDUCATION\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
